condition_name: Colorectal Cancer
condition_slug: colorectal-cancer
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Second most frequent cancer in males (after prostate cancer) and 4 inth both sexes (after breast, cervical and prostatic cancers), constituting 5.8% of all new cancer cases in Nigeria."
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Elective
    features[7]: change in bowel habits,abdominal swelling,abdominal pain,tenesmus,weight loss,anaemia,secondary haemorrhoids
  - type: Emergency
    features[4]: large bowel intestinal obstruction,perforation with peritonitis,lower gastrointestinal haemorrhage,"fistulae (recto-vesical, recto-vaginal)"
investigations[16]: Colonoscopy and biopsy,barium enema,Abdominopelvic USS,Abdominopelvic CT scan,Chest X-ray/CT,IVU,Cystoscopy,Haematological tests,Biochemical tests,Tumour markers (CEA),Electrocardiogram,Echocardiography,Digital rectal examination,"Faecal tests (occult blood test, immunochemical test, DNA testing)",Colonoscopy,Double contrast barium enema
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[13]: 5-day whole gut lavage,3-day whole gut lavage,1-day whole gut lavage,on-table lavage (in emergency situations),Erythromycin,Neomycin,Thalazole,Metronidazole,5 Fluoro-uracil,Folinic acid,Oxaliplatin,Irinotecan,Capecitabine
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[0]:
prevention[7]: Adenomatous polyps,familial polyposis coli,Dietary risk factors,Obesity,Sedentary lifestyle,Schistosomiasis,uretero-sigmoidostomy
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment[13]: right hemicolectomy,transverse colectomy,left hemicolectomy,sigmoid colectomy,anterior resection,abdomino-perineal resection with terminal colostomy,sphincter-saving excision,"abdomino-perineal resection with terminal colostomy, excision plus chemoradiation",Isolated hepatic metastatectomy,Emergency surgery for obstruction/perforation (resection +/- colostomy),Rx for lower gastrointestinal haemorrhage,Targeted therapy,"Radiotherapy (Post-surgery, Palliative care, Chemo-radiation for anal carcinoma)"
prognosis: null